\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Comparative spectral convergence study across 6 refinement levels ($N \in \{9$, $13$, $17$, $21$, $25$, $29\}$) under spatial and directional disorder: (a) Mean relative spectral error in cutoff wavenumber $k_c$ (\%) as a function of total active degrees of freedom $N_{\mathrm  {DoF}}$; (b) Convergence rate as a function of characteristic DoF spacing $h_{\mathrm  {DoF}} = \sqrt  {|\Omega |/N_{\mathrm  {DoF}}}$. The regular grid exhibits an observed fitted slope of $\mathcal  {O}(h_{\mathrm  {DoF}}^{2.80})$, while the irregular cloud ($25\%$ spatial jitter and random director orientations $\theta _k \in [0, 2\pi )$) exhibits an observed fitted slope of $\mathcal  {O}(h_{\mathrm  {DoF}}^{2.20})$ across the evaluated single-realization sequence, which is empirically compatible with the expected behavior of a complete linear polynomial approximation.}}{73}{figure.217}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convergencia_cavidade_aleatoria}{{9}{73}{Comparative spectral convergence study across 6 refinement levels ($N \in \{9$, $13$, $17$, $21$, $25$, $29\}$) under spatial and directional disorder: (a) Mean relative spectral error in cutoff wavenumber $k_c$ (\%) as a function of total active degrees of freedom $N_{\mathrm {DoF}}$; (b) Convergence rate as a function of characteristic DoF spacing $h_{\mathrm {DoF}} = \sqrt {|\Omega |/N_{\mathrm {DoF}}}$. The regular grid exhibits an observed fitted slope of $\mathcal {O}(h_{\mathrm {DoF}}^{2.80})$, while the irregular cloud ($25\%$ spatial jitter and random director orientations $\theta _k \in [0, 2\pi )$) exhibits an observed fitted slope of $\mathcal {O}(h_{\mathrm {DoF}}^{2.20})$ across the evaluated single-realization sequence, which is empirically compatible with the expected behavior of a complete linear polynomial approximation}{figure.217}{}}
